  "levels_won_this_session": [5],
  "novel_mechanics_found": "LEVEL 5 solved: route the latched 8/12 assembly a second time so its color-12 slab occupies columns 10-13, rows 22-33, creating a bridge from the lower checker stack to the previously isolated solid F socket. Stepping onto that socket reveals a hidden F button at (52,15); it swaps solidity between the vertical F chute and the lower horizontal F bar. After descending the solid chute, a B-shelf at columns 22-27 spans both endpoints and supports the avatar while the F button is toggled back, making the horizontal bar walkable to the B goal. LEVEL 6 scouting: standing on its color-8 socket reveals another hidden 8 control; its large 6 control rotates the large color-12 structure even without teleporting, and its B control cycles three lower shelves through positions and material states.",
  "narrative": "The required 212-label prefix reached frame.levels_completed=4 from two fresh resets. The first level-5 probe reproduced prior routing and then confirmed the known row-44 endpoint soft-lock, using 319 calls. From a second fresh reset I replayed the prefix, used an optimized route to physically investigate the unexplained upper F socket, discovered its hidden control, solved the two-phase F transfer puzzle, and observed frame.levels_completed advance live from 4 to 5 at action 322 of the recorded reset-rooted sequence. I continued into level 6 and grounded several controls, but its revealed 8 control remained condition-gated. I stopped at 685 total calls; reproduction_verified is false because replaying the 322-action candidate in reproduce() would exceed the 700-call session cap.",
  "gotchas": [
    "Direction mapping: ACTION1=up, ACTION2=down, ACTION3=left, ACTION4=right; every move is 2 pixels (sprites are 2x2 on a 2x-upscaled grid).",
    "The rendered frame may be a stack with shape (2,64,64); use the last frame for the current 2D grid.",
    "The AA99 controls move the 8 object rather than rotating it; the fourth quadrant at (59,29) is down and the previously missed quadrant at (54,29) is right.",
    "The 8 button only visibly latches after the 8 object is aligned against the color-12 slab; after latching, direction controls drag both as one assembly.",
    "To bridge the initial vertical gap: latch at the upper-right alignment, move the assembly left to its limit, down three times, then right until the color-12 slab spans rows 22-33; walk left onto the slab before climbing because its right edge is not walkable from the fixed pad.",
    "Restore the assembly before climbing to the top checker: left to the limit, up three, then right three.",
    "The 2-button cycle is reversible and has a distinct all-color-12 full-bridge phase after the fully walled phase; map it while on the fixed west pad and cross only at the full phase.",
    "Further 2-button clicks after crossing close the bridge from the middle and can trap the avatar on the east endpoint because the final support-deleting closure is refused.",
    "For the F solve, route the assembly to columns 10-13 / rows 22-33 after teleporting to the lower checker, then climb onto the solid F socket; merely clicking the socket does not reveal its control.",
    "The hidden F button appears at (52,15) only after the avatar physically steps onto the upper F socket.",
    "Shift the lower B shelf exactly four times to columns 22-27. Color 1 is walkable there; a fifth shift to columns 24-29 leaves no overlap with the horizontal F bar and was the misleading prior dead end.",
    "Descend the solid F chute, walk left twice on the columns-22-27 shelf, then toggle F back and climb onto the now-solid horizontal bar.",
    "On level 6, stepping onto the color-8 socket at the upper edge of the isolated lower-right pad reveals a hidden 8 control, but direct clicks in the scouted configurations were no-ops.",
    "Blocked moves and refused support-deleting toggles consume env.step budget and advance the visible row-63 tick counter."
  ],
